    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For each c=1 parity source branch, the constant gate is h_Xj=sP with s^2=-epsilon. Eliminating r against r^4-2xr^2+1 collapses the six roles to four explicit polynomials: R0, common R1/R2, P0, and common P1/P2. The even x-sign norm then gives exactly seven degree-2^36 Jacobi gcds per torsion sign. All fourteen tests share the existing CR-002 order-2^39 minus norm and 37-level plus tower. Absence of official divisors of both norms empties the full generic two-antipodal c=1 parity packet; compatible divisors still require scalar and Euclidean replay.",
